Well, I just YASD'd my best game ever. After a year and a half, I'm
beginning to think I'll never ascend.

Had a very promising samurai named Largo. Did the mines first (don't
ask me why, I usually start with Soko - I started the game months ago
and abandoned it; when I reloaded I was hallucinating in the mines. I
do know why I was hallucinating, though - I had been experimenting
with a junkie conduct - inducing hallucination and confusion in myself
whenever items presented me with the chance. Largo spent most of Mines
stoned out of his head, having accrued something like 1000 turns of
hallucination). Was having trouble staying unburdened, but Soko's
prize was a BoH, which helped a lot. I had an early CoMR, which I
enchanted up to +5. I would have had more enchanted armor, but it took
me ages to find a scroll of enchant armor and so most of my blank
scrolls were turning into ID to find out what the crap my other
scrolls and potions and rings were. I had AoLS's, and used them both
up. Once I got in a fight with a leocrotta, and was very confused when
it kicked my ass, considering I had thought I could two-hit kill them.
The second one went when I was blowing some create monster wands at an
altar and got a horde. There was something nasty in it,and it got me.
I had a few other close calls and was wasting pets like mad until I
found a polytrap and acquired a Marilith. I went on the quest for my
first time EVER, and about 3 levels in I realized that AC -4 just
wasn't going to cut it. Luckily I found a green dragon (I think it was
a wolf that got polytrapped) and made some scale mail, bringing my AC
down to -8. I tamed a kitten, polytrapped it into a white dragon, and
decided to wait before finishing the quest because I didn't know how
hard the nemesis would be.

A levelporter warped my Marilith away, and I decided to go on without
her. I blew up my bag of holding by putting in an un-ID'd wand (just a
few minutes after I thought "gee, I'd better not put that in my BoH,"
actually...I named my CoMR "balsa wands are CANCELLATION" after that.)
Got to Medusa and had no wand of cold, levitation, water walking, or
magical breathing, so I dug down to the maze level below. Next level
after was the castle. I didn't know the tune or have any way to cross
the water (I had had some ?oEarth, but they were in the BoH) so I
tried to dig down again but the ground was too hard. Well... crap. I
didn't fancy sitting around on the castle level, so I decided to go
up, patiently look for better armor (my gloves were only +1, and my
boots and helmet were +0), then finish the quest and see whether I had
a way to cross the water yet or not. So I went up the stairs to
Medusa's level.

I had some vague memory of her down stairs being on an island off to
the right, but I must have been mistaken. I came out next to Medusa.
My dragon got the first turn and he put up a valiant fight, but
couldn't kill Medusa before she met his gaze and stoned him. Of
course, I was stoned too. DYWYPI?

The inventory ID showed that I didn't have any way to become voluntary-
blind anyway, and in truth I couldn't remember ever having seen a
towel or blindfold this game, which is odd because I usually have too
many. I guess I should have kept a !ofBlindness on hand, but I hadn't
thought I'd need it when I diluted the only one I remember having many
levels before, and all the ones I'd seen since had been hurtling
through the air at my face. So even had I known that Medusa would be
standing right there, it would only have meant that I got to sit
around on two levels, with one wand of create monster that I'd found
since my BoH explosion and no altar, waiting for more equipment. Ugh.

That six-digit score is making my other scores (mostly in the lower 5-
digit range) look bad. Grr...



